**Definition 1.1 (specimen, output and error).** There is one unknown
normalized original reached-cut specimen $E\rho_{y,e,n}E^\dagger$, where
$E:\mathbb C^3\to\mathbb C^5$ is the calibrated isometry, $P=EE^\dagger$,
and

$$
\begin{aligned}
p_y&=(y/128,(64-y)/128,1/2),&
a_y&=(\sqrt{p_{y0}},\sqrt{p_{y1}},\sqrt{p_{y2}})^T,\\
\rho_{y,e,n}&=U_{e,n}a_ya_y^TU_{e,n}^\dagger,&
U_{e,n}&=\operatorname{diag}(e,n,1),\\
y&\in\{5,16,27\},&e,n&\in\{+1,-1\}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{TA.1}
$$

The original height is $y/256$ and winding parity is $en=(-1)^m$.
The ideal output $\Omega_{y,e,n}$ has the complete coherent live block
specified by CG.111 and five separate original failure measures, in label
order $(0,1,2,3,13)$,

$$
w_\ell f_y(t)dt\,P_f,\qquad
w=(0,1/4,1/2,1/4,0),\qquad f_y(t)=\frac{6y}{(y+6t)^2}.
\tag{TA.2}
$$

The error is HALF the full stopped-cq trace norm,

$$
E(\Phi)=\max_{y,e,n}\frac12
 \|\Phi(E\rho_{y,e,n}E^\dagger)-\Omega_{y,e,n}\|_{1,\mathrm{cq}}.
\tag{TA.3}
$$

It includes every live coherence, singular-time, abort, wrong-support,
zero-ideal and additional sector. The simulator density
$g(t)=2/(1+t)^2$ is distinct from the ideal $f_y$.

